Build the payment infrastructure powering global commerce.
Boku connects billions of consumers to the payment methods they prefer, one market at a time. Our platform connects the world’s leading digital businesses to the local payment methods their customers already use. Spotify, Meta, Microsoft, Netflix and Tencent already run on Boku’s payment infrastructure. We operate across 60+ countries, support 200+ local payment methods and reach 7.5 billion consumer accounts.
With headquarters in London and San Francisco and colleagues working across markets around the world, Boku is global by default. From London to Mumbai, São Paulo to Singapore, our teams collaborate across time zones, markets and cultures to build products for customers around the world.
Join us to solve complex, real-time payment challenges at global scale. We share knowledge freely, take ownership of complexity and look for people who question how things are done and find better ways to build.
Role Purpose&nbsp;
The Marketing Operations Manager owns the systems, data and processes that power how Boku Marketing operates globally and how Marketing feeds the wider go-to-market motion. This hands-on role combines deep technical expertise with strategic, commercial leadership: building a trusted MarTech foundation, improving marketing influence and attribution, and turning campaigns into measurable pipeline and revenue impact. The role works closely with Demand Generation, Sales and Revenue Operations to deliver scalable campaign operations, disciplined lead management and practical AI-enabled ways of working.&nbsp;
Key Responsibilities&nbsp;
Own and continuously improve the operating model, technology and data that enable Marketing to plan, execute and measure high-impact global activity.&nbsp;
• MarTech stack and architecture: Own the end-to-end marketing technology stack, anchored on Salesforce and Account Engagement. Configure, document and optimise integrations, data flows, permissions and processes so the stack is reliable, scalable and easy for teams to use.
• Marketing influence, attribution and reporting: Build and evolve marketing influence and attribution models that connect programmes and touchpoints to pipeline and revenue. Establish reporting standards and actionable dashboards for campaign performance, funnel conversion, contribution and ROI.
• Lead lifecycle management: Design and maintain the trackable path from initial signal and conversion capture through enrichment, scoring and qualification to sales handover, opportunity creation and revenue. Partner with Revenue Operations to define service levels and measure lead-to-opportunity performance.
• Lead scoring and data strategy: Build and iterate fit, engagement and intent scoring models. Own data hygiene, enrichment, segmentation, consent and governance practices, including GDPR and applicable regional requirements.
• Campaign and event operations: Build and optimise event, email and nurture campaigns in Account Engagement. Partner with marketing stakeholders to create repeatable campaign workflows, audience logic, tracking and post-campaign measurement.
• ABM operations: Enable our account-based marketing approach through account selection, segmentation, buying-group data, account journeys, orchestration and measurement in close partnership with Demand Generation, Sales and Channel Marketing.
• AI and workflow automation: Turn AI into practical improvements by automating recurring work, reducing manual effort and improving quality. Build and maintain Marketing’s AI standardisation framework, including approved tools, prompt libraries, review standards and data handling rules.
• Marketing operating cadence: Support marketing leadership to define strategic initiatives, targets and OKRs; manage the operational cadence and leadership reviews; track budget and progress; and unblock cross-functional initiatives across demand generation, channel marketing and brand.
• Process improvement and delivery: Drive operational efficiency by identifying friction, establishing best-practice project management methods and coordinating high-priority integrated campaigns across content, events and ABM.
• Team enablement and adoption: training programmes, playbooks, documentation, office hours, new-user onboarding, and using adoption feedback to improve processes.
Measures of Success&nbsp;
• Trusted marketing data: agreed data-quality standards, documented governance and measurable improvement in completeness, accuracy and compliance.&nbsp;
• Lead lifecycle performance: visible conversion and velocity from MQL through sales acceptance, opportunity creation, pipeline and revenue.&nbsp;
• Effective scoring and handover: scoring model and service-level performance regularly reviewed with Revenue Operations and Sales, with actions taken to improve quality and follow-up.&nbsp;
• Campaign and event operational excellence: campaigns launched accurately, on time and with consistent audience, tracking, consent and reporting standards.&nbsp;
• Marketing contribution insight: influence and attribution reporting used in leadership decisions, with clear visibility of programme contribution to pipeline and revenue.&nbsp;
• Operational leverage: practical AI and workflow automation adopted for priority processes, reducing manual effort while maintaining quality and data-handling standards. Training, playbooks, and measurable user adoption&nbsp;
Key Skills, experience and Competencies &nbsp;
• Salesforce and Account Engagement expertise: Advanced hands-on experience designing, building and optimising marketing automation, CRM processes, integrations, reporting and governance.&nbsp;
• B2B marketing operations: Demonstrated experience in high-growth payments, SaaS or technology environments, supporting demand generation, channel marketing, ABM and brand teams.&nbsp;
• Attribution and analytics: Strong analytical capability, with the ability to translate complex funnel, campaign and revenue metrics into clear business insights and decisions.&nbsp;
• Lead management and data governance: Experience developing lead scoring, lifecycle, enrichment and handover frameworks, alongside strong knowledge of data quality, privacy and GDPR.&nbsp;
• Campaign and ABM execution: Hands-on expertise building email, nurture and event campaigns, with a deep understanding of ABM strategy, audience operations and measurement.&nbsp;
• AI and automation: Practical experience identifying high-value automation opportunities and applying AI responsibly through repeatable workflows, standards and controls.&nbsp;
• Programme leadership and influence: Able to lead operational cadences, manage competing priorities and influence cross-functional stakeholders without direct authority in a fast-paced environment.&nbsp;
• Enablement and training. Ability to turn technical capabilities into practical guidance and training for marketing team.&nbsp;
Qualifications
• No formal qualification is essential; min 7 years equivalent practical experience in marketing operations, revenue operations or marketing technology is required.&nbsp;
• Salesforce and/or Account Engagement certifications, or demonstrable equivalent hands-on expertise.&nbsp;

Job Purpose
The Customer Support Advisor is responsible for investigating and resolving customer queries and complaints relating to the handling and progress of their claim. Working closely with internal teams and external parties, the role ensures fair outcomes, clear communication, and a high standard of customer service.
Key Responsibilities
• Handle customer queries in an efficient and effective manner to ensure the continual contribution to the firm’s quality of all services offered;
• Ensure customers are treated fairly and in accordance with all Company policies and procedures;
• Monitor the Customer Support Team results to ensure there is a continual contribution to the firm’s quality of all services offered.
• Assist with the administration and investigation of customer queries, including liaison with all appropriate internal and external parties to secure the relevant information to quickly deal with and resolve the query;
• Contact customers by all appropriate means to gain a full understanding of their query in order to progress the issue to a fair outcome and resolution as quickly as possible;
• Keep up to date with all insurance, claims and legal developments and procedures and internal processes;
• Assist in the identification of any risk, training or performance needs, both within the team, department and businesswide;
• Contribute to continuous improvement within the Customer Support function;
Experience & Knowledge
• Experience in the conduct of insurance claims notification and handling processes and/or personal injury claims handling and litigation;
• A strong awareness of good customer service and Treating Customers Fairly;
• Attention to detail and able to interpret information, make sound decisions and take ownership of issues to resolution;
• Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, both written and oral.
• Organised, time management skills and an ability to work under pressure and flexibly to meet business deadlines;
• Strong IT/case management skills;
Desirables
• Ability to interpret information, identify risk and provide feedback in a clear and concise manner;
• A customer service qualification or a willingness to undertake progress towards a recognised and relevant qualification;
• A knowledge and experience of ISO frameworks, including ISO10002;
Here at Carpenters group diversity and inclusion matters, it is integral to our culture and we welcome applications from everyone. We celebrate difference and believe in equal opportunities for all. Due to the high volume of applications we receive for certain roles, we may close vacancies earlier than the advertised date. We therefore encourage you to submit your application as soon as possible.
About us
Here at Carpenters Group, we’ve been providing legal and insurance services across the UK for over 30 years. We’ve grown from a small law firm into a 1500 people strong team made up of insurance professionals, legal experts and best in class corporate services, working across seven office locations. We work in partnership with household name insurers to deliver a variety of fully outsourced claim solutions. We also represent individuals who need expert legal support.
As a great place to work our core values underpin how we behave. Our working environment is positive and informal, and we encourage people to work together to perform at their best.
We understand that our success as a business depends on the success of our people, which is why we invest in your training, development and social projects, helping everyone to connect and grow.
No matter what stage of your career, at Carpenters Group there is a place for you to achieve your potential.
Benefits
• 25 days' holiday per annum
• Holiday buy and sell scheme
• Hybrid working model (in relevant role)
• 2 x Volunteering days to support charitable initiatives
• Matched Giving – up to £250 matched for personal charity fundraising for a registered charity
• Medicash cash plan – claim back dental / physio / optical appointments
• My Medicash App – including access to rapid digital physiotherapy and skin cancer screening assessments plus fitness videos and wellbeing tools
• Discounts and cash back on travel and shopping through Medicash extras
• Life Assurance Scheme (4 x salary)
• Pension scheme
• Funded driving theory test (in relevant role)
• Active network of Wellbeing Champions – providing mental health support
• Training and development opportunities
• Funded social events to connect with your colleagues
• Dress for your day policy

Job title: Head of News
Location: Highstreet Kensington, London
&nbsp;&nbsp;
The i Paper is appointing a Head of News to lead its ambitious news operation. This&nbsp;pivotal&nbsp;role is responsible for delivering political scoops, high-impact investigations and agenda-setting exclusives to grow The i Paper's digital audience and deepen subscriber engagement. Leading a team of award-winning editors and reporters, the Head of News is an experienced digital specialist with the ability to develop and&nbsp;execute&nbsp;complex news projects across formats including social video.&nbsp;
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
Key responsibilities:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
-Drive and deliver ambitious&nbsp;and&nbsp;distinctive news projects&nbsp;across&nbsp;all&nbsp;The i Paper’s platforms&nbsp;
-Conceive and&nbsp;own&nbsp;high-impact investigations and agenda-setting exclusives&nbsp;
-Support and expand the use of social video to deepen the impact of storytelling&nbsp;
-Ensure a&nbsp;daily&nbsp;focus on identifying and delivering content that differentiates The i Paper from its competitors&nbsp;&nbsp;
-Effective people management, developing our newsroom talent with strength and diplomacy&nbsp;
-Lead strong news planning to develop subscriber content, with robust organisation and cross-newsroom creativity&nbsp;&nbsp;
-Ensure use of data-driven insights across the newsroom, using metrics to inspire ideas&nbsp;&nbsp;
-Support&nbsp;the development,&nbsp;execution&nbsp;and success of&nbsp;The i Paper's award-winning campaigns&nbsp;
-Work with audience colleagues to develop new multi-platform content, improving digital storytelling across The i Paper's channels&nbsp;&nbsp;
-Ensure all news&nbsp;publishing&nbsp;is accurate and adheres to the highest standards, building and maintaining The i Paper's reputation for trustworthy reporting&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
-Oversee management of the news rota, helping to plan staffing for major news events as required&nbsp;&nbsp;
&nbsp;&nbsp;
Key skills and qualifications:&nbsp;&nbsp;
-Proven experience in a senior news editorial role, with a strong background in digital journalism&nbsp;
-Strong track record of delivering exclusive stories and investigations&nbsp;that drive audience engagement&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
-Excellent leadership and team management skills, with the ability to inspire and mentor a large&nbsp;team&nbsp;&nbsp;
-Deep understanding of digital media trends and audience behaviour&nbsp;&nbsp;
-Exceptional writing, editing and communication skills&nbsp;&nbsp;
-Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, deadline-driven environment&nbsp;&nbsp;
Package Description
&nbsp;
Our benefits package increases the longer you’ve been with us. Here’s what to expect:
• 25 days’ holiday (increasing by 1 per year up to a total of 30)
• Pension plan and life cover
• Discounts on online shopping, dining cards and vouchers, and access to our Employee Assistance Programme
• Onsite gym, subsidised canteen and onsite nurse and GP clinics
Plus much more...
THE I PAPER
The i Paper is the only national newspaper that's never supported a political party and it reaches more than [9.2] million readers each month in print and online.&nbsp;
It is committed to delivering accurate, impartial news and intelligent debate, trusting readers to make up their own minds. It is the winner of 2024 UK Newspaper of the Year and is rapidly growing its digital subscriptions base, recently hitting [70k] total subscriptions.
www.theipaper.com
Our Commitment
We are committed to increasing diversity and maintaining an inclusive workplace culture. We welcome applications from all qualified candidates regardless of their ethnicity, race, gender, religious beliefs, sexual orientation, age, marital status, or disability.
We are Disability Confident Committed. Please let us know if you require any recruitment documentation in other formats or if you require reasonable adjustments to be made during the recruitment process. Please be assured that any such information will be held separately to your recruitment application and will not be considered as part of the selection process.

Fitch Ratings is seeking a Credit Analyst to join its EMEA Energy, Natural Resources & Infrastructure team based out of London or Manchester.
Fitch Ratings’ EMEA Corporates, Infrastructure and Project Finance group provides public and private ratings of companies, debt instruments, project finance and infrastructure transactions across Europe, the Middle East and Africa. Its team of more than 100 credit analysts is based in London, Frankfurt, Paris, Warsaw, Madrid, Barcelona, Milan, Stockholm and Dubai.
The Corporates group comprises six sector teams: Energy, Natural Resources & Infrastructure; Utilities; Consumer and Healthcare; Industrials; Telecoms, Media and Technology, Services and Leveraged Finance; and Real Estate.
The EMEA Energy, Natural Resources & Infrastructure team covers around 200 public and private ratings across oil and gas, metals and mining, chemicals and fertilisers, energy project finance, infrastructure and transport. Its analysts are based in London, Frankfurt, Barcelona, Madrid, Warsaw, Milan and Dubai.
What We Offer:
• Manage issuer coverage at a global rating agency
• Develop expertise across corporates and project finance
• Engage with EMEA corporates, investors and bankers
• Join a successful, diverse and international team
We’ll Count on You To:
• Monitor a portfolio of commodities companies and infrastructure issuers and identify developments requiring rating action;
• Support lead analysts with research, financial modelling and presentation to rating committees;
• Participate in meetings with issuers’ executive management;
• Conduct quantitative analysis, including comprehensive financial statement forecasting;
• Conduct qualitative analysis of business models, competitive strengths, management strategy, industry dynamics and regulation;
• Contribute to thematic research in your coverage sectors;
• Work in accordance with all relevant policies and procedures;
• Foster open discussion, collaboration and a strong team culture.
What You Need to Have:
• Bachelor’s degree required; MBA or other advanced degree preferred;
• At least 3 years’ experience in credit, financial analysis or accounting, with a strong understanding of financial statements;
• Knowledge of the Energy, Natural Resources and Infrastructure sector preferred;
• Strong analytical and quantitative skills;
• Strong critical thinking and a keen interest in AI;
• Project finance expertise a plus;
• Excellent written and verbal English; additional languages are advantageous;
• Ability to manage multiple projects and adapt as priorities change;
• Ability to thrive in a team-oriented environment.
Why Fitch?
At Fitch Group, the combined power of our global perspectives is what differentiates us. Our global network of colleagues comes together to accomplish things greater than they ever could alone.
Every team member is essential to our business and each perspective is critical to our success. We embrace a diverse culture that encourages a free exchange of ideas, guaranteeing your voice will be heard and your work will have an impact, regardless of seniority.
We are building incredible things at Fitch and we invite you to join us on our journey.
Fitch Ratings is a leading provider of credit ratings, commentary and research. Dedicated to providing value beyond the rating through independent and prospective credit opinions, Fitch ratings offers global perspectives shaped by strong local market experience and credit market expertise. The additional context, perspective and insights we provide have helped fund a century of growth and enables our clients to make important credit judgements with confidence.
Fitch Group is a global leader in financial information services with operations in more than 30 countries. Wholly owned by the Hearst Corporation, we are comprised of three main businesses: Fitch Ratings | Fitch Solutions | Fitch Learning.
For more information please visit our websites: www.fitchratings.com | www.fitchsolutions.com | www.fitchlearning.com
Fitch is committed to providing global securities markets with objective, timely, independent and forward-looking credit opinions. To protect Fitch’s credibility and reputation, our employees must take every precaution to avoid conflicts of interests or any appearance of a conflict of interest. Should you be successful in the recruitment process at Fitch Ratings you will be asked to declare any securities holdings and other potential conflicts prior to commencing employment. If you, or your immediate family, have any holdings that may conflict with your work responsibilities, you may be asked to divest yourself of them before beginning work.
Fitch Group is proud to be an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. We evaluate qualified applicants without regard to race, color, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability, protected veteran status, and other statuses protected by law.
