Purpose of the role:
You will be required to attend appointments/bookings at various locations in a company van (provided) to resolve or perform maintenance functions and inspections. You will assess, install and fix or fit equipment (tail lifts, Roller Doors etc) and/or supply parts as required.
Key responsibilities:
- Report directly into the Aftersales Manager or any other person as directed by the General Manager and/or any director of the Company;
- Undertake all service, repair and refurbishment work that the Company schedules for you in accordance with its main business of aftersales and repair work for commercial vehicle bodies, tail lifts, crash cushions and other lifting equipment, including, without limitation, carrying out service work, scheduled repair and maintenance and breakdowns;
- Maintain your Company van in a tidy and efficient manner to enable safe working and facilitate stock takes, including without limitation (i) undertaking and recording daily, weekly and monthly checks for the van’s maintenance and (ii) providing feedback to the Operations Manager in relation to any potential issues with the van or equipment on the van;
- Work with company provided PDA or other device in order to accurately reflect the work undertaken during your working week, including clocking on and off sites of work, noting travelling time, reporting time taken to perform tasks and photographing all jobs undertaken as required to enable the company to provide estimates and/or obtain order numbers;
- Where required by your line manager and/or other supervisor, provide detailed information and advice in order to enable the Company to provide accurate quotations for repair work;
- Provide a timesheet detailing your week’s work prior to 10am each Monday morning;
- Communicate professionally with customers of the Company;
- Communicate regularly and professionally with the Company’s office staff;
- Provide regular feedback to the Operation Manager regarding performance;
- Control expenses to meet budget guidelines, both of yourself and of the company’s engineers;
- Adhere to all company policies (including wearing of uniform), procedures and business ethics codes; and
- Undertaking all other tasks required by your line manager and/or any of the Company’s board of directors.
In keeping with accepted principles of good working practice, you may be required to undertake additional or alternative duties.
Relationships and Roles:
- Work with other company employees to achieve sales strategy and Company goals, including with respect to upselling of parts to ensure maximum profitability for the Company;
- Wear all company provided clothing and personal protective equipment, and at all times maintain a high standard of dress in accordance with the company’s image; and
- Maintain contact with all customers in the market area to ensure high levels of customer satisfaction, reporting current issues to the board of directors as required.
Behavioral Requirements:
- Adhere to all company policies, procedures and business ethics codes.
- Have a high standard and concern for excellence
- Problem solving ability
- Good communication skills
- Good time Management
- Highly motivated
- Ability to work as part of a team
- Responsible for cleanliness and housekeeping standards in own area
- Honest and determined
- Ability to work on own initiative
- To be able to follow instructions and abide by Health and Safety regulations
- Reliable
- Positive “can do” attitude
- A desire to work in pressurised, fast paced environment

&nbsp;
About Netcraft
Netcraft is the global leader in cybercrime detection and disruption. We’re a trusted partner for three of the four largest companies in the world and many large governments. We've blocked over 225 million cyber-attacks to date, and we take down around 33% of the world's phishing attacks.
Our purpose and passion are focused on just one thing: protecting the world from cybercrime.
That passion shapes how we work, too. We’re proud of our talented team and the value each person brings, and we’ve built a workplace where people feel supported and inspired. From strong benefits and wellness programs to meaningful collaboration and team connection.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
The Role
We're seeking a Cybercrime Analyst to join our amazing Technical Operations team. Cybercrime Analysts have an opportunity to make a real difference in the world by identifying threats and acting to protect governments, banks, and consumers from online attacks. You'll be a key part of the incident response team, finding innovative ways to rapidly disrupt cyber-attacks against our clients. And don't worry if you have limited experience in this area: we can train you.
Day to day, your responsibilities will include:
• Cybercrime incident response – communicating analysis of cyber threats to relevant parties to mitigate attacks;
• Classification of malicious websites, social media profiles, apps, emails, and phone numbers;
• Providing clear and professional feedback to customers on incidents and classifications;
• Sharing your ideas on how to improve processes and workflows.
Based at our Bath office, but with hybrid flexibility, you’ll report directly to a more senior member of the Technical Operations function and will work closely with colleagues across different teams.&nbsp;
To be successful, you’ll need
• Attention to detail, adaptability, and strong intellectual and commercial curiosity;
• A positive and solution-focused approach;
• Interest in the internet and cybercrime prevention;
• Excellent communication skills with a high standard of written English;
• Ability to engage with people in a friendly, helpful, and professional way;
• Self-motivation, ability to take initiative, and work as part of a team;
• Aptitude for analysing and using technical information;
• Competence in handling incoming phone calls;
• Some experience in cybersecurity is useful but not essential as full training will be provided;
• A degree in Cyber Security, Computer Science, IT, or any field that promotes analytical thinking may be beneficial but is not essential.&nbsp;
Prior experience or knowledge in cybersecurity is not required; we’re more interested in your passion and willingness to grow in this field.&nbsp;
Your standard working days will be Wednesday to Sunday, or Saturday to Wednesday.
While there is some room for flexibility in choosing workdays, it is required that weekends are worked. This is because Netcraft protects its customers 24/7, 365 days per year, which we'll discuss with you at interview. Following the training period, a minimum of two days per week in the office will be required.
The Reward Package:
• A salary of £30,000, reviewed annually
• 33 days annual leave - includes public holidays which can be worked if you prefer
• Enhanced Sick Pay from day 1, rising to 12 weeks full pay after 6 months
• Salary sacrifice pension with matched employer contributions up to 5% + NI savings
• Vitality Private health cover, including access to a private GP service
• Life Assurance at 4 x salary
• Generous enhanced Parental leave and pay entitlements
• Equity tracking scheme (eligibility criteria apply) - allowing you share in Netcraft's long term success
• (Sonder) Comprehensive health, safety, and wellness service available 24/7 for you and your family
• Two paid Learning &amp; Development days per year plus access to learning resources such as Udemy and Coursera to support your career
• Two Volunteering Days per year, to allow you to contribute to your wider community or charity
• Meals, snacks, and drinks provided daily in the office
• Employee Referral Bonus scheme
• Hybrid and flexible working options
• Spot reward bonus scheme to reward truly outstanding contributions&nbsp;
Diversity, Equity &amp; Inclusion&nbsp;
This is deeply important to us. Through our ally network, we support under-represented groups and&nbsp;maintain&nbsp;a working environment free from bias, harassment, or discrimination. We encourage candidates from all backgrounds to apply.&nbsp;
We’re also happy to make adjustments to the hiring process to ensure every candidate can participate fully.&nbsp;
Please note: Netcraft does not accept unsolicited approaches from external recruiters.&nbsp;

